`.github/workflows/security.yml` has two tiers. **Enforcing** (blocks merges; every run, including the one CI calls first): gitleaks over the full history, then `./scripts/security-checks.sh` — the same gate as on a laptop. **Advisory** (log-only; weekly cron, manual dispatch and docs-only pushes): Semgrep, Trivy, a Syft SBOM. Every scanner is a pinned release verified by sha256 (`scripts/fetch-pinned-release.sh`) — never `curl … | sh`, never bumped without the procedure. → `docs/conventions/security-workflow.md`
